00:45:25.350 --> 00:45:31.450
Ravi, played by Sentil Ramamurthy, who also was in the show Heroes, I want to point out
由森德希·拉玛莫西饰演的拉维时，他同时也出演过《英雄》，我想指出的是

1064
00:45:31.450 --> 00:45:37.070
that in an earlier episode, The Negotiation, I think, Dwight mentions hero Nakamura from
在更早的一集《谈判》中，我想德怀特提到了《英雄》里的英雄中村，

1065
00:45:37.070 --> 00:45:42.030
Heroes, which means the show exists in Dwight's life on The Office.
这意味着《英雄》这部剧在德怀特生活的《办公室》世界里是真实存在的。

1066
00:45:42.490 --> 00:45:45.590
Wouldn't Dwight have also recognized Ravi from Heroes?
难道德怀特不应该认出拉维就是《英雄》里的演员吗？

1067
00:45:45.950 --> 00:45:46.670
I wish.
我也希望如此。

1068
00:45:46.670 --> 00:45:50.210
I wish there was a moment where he walked by and did a double take, like, hmm?
我真希望有个镜头是他走过去时回头看了一眼，心想，嗯？

1069
00:45:50.690 --> 00:45:50.970
Yeah.
是啊。

1070
00:45:51.470 --> 00:45:56.990
This was when we sort of gave up on the fact that people were well known for other shows.
这大概就是我们放弃纠结演员在其他剧中是否出名这件事的时候了。

1071
00:45:58.150 --> 00:46:02.850
Ryan actually ends up going up to Jim and Pam because he wants more info on the situation
瑞安实际上跑去问吉姆和帕姆，因为他想了解更多情况，

1072
00:46:02.850 --> 00:46:05.510
because it seems like this guy is really into Kelly.
因为看起来这家伙真的很迷凯莉。

1073
00:46:05.810 --> 00:46:10.450
And Ryan would rather Kelly be alone than be with somebody, even though they weren't right
瑞安宁愿凯莉单身也不愿她和别人在一起，尽管他们当时并没有在一起。

1074
00:46:10.450 --> 00:46:10.830
together.
然后他问，这是爱情吗？

1075
00:46:11.530 --> 00:46:13.570
And then he's like, is this love?
天哪。

1076
00:46:14.070 --> 00:46:14.730
Oh my God.
我的天。

1077
00:46:14.870 --> 00:46:15.410
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

1078
00:46:15.410 --> 00:46:16.350
Pam's look to Ryan.
帕姆看向瑞安的眼神。

1079
00:46:16.610 --> 00:46:16.730
Yeah.
是啊。

1080
00:46:17.510 --> 00:46:23.950
Well, now Robert and Andy are going to go into Nellie's office and Robert's going to say,
好了，现在罗伯特和安迪要走进奈莉的办公室，罗伯特要说，

1081
00:46:24.070 --> 00:46:26.890
listen, you know, you've been great, but Andy is the manager.
听着，你知道，你一直表现得很好，但安迪才是经理。

1082
00:46:27.270 --> 00:46:28.750
And Nellie's like, no.
而奈莉说，不行。

1083
00:46:29.910 --> 00:46:31.850
This throws Robert for a loop.
这让罗伯特感到措手不及。

1084
00:46:31.970 --> 00:46:34.090
He says he is not used to being told no.
他说他不习惯被人拒绝。

1085
00:46:34.390 --> 00:46:39.230
And then Nellie is very flirty with him and she's like, get used to it because it's
然后奈莉对他非常调情，她说，习惯就好，因为当有人说愿意时，那种感觉会非常美妙，

1086
00:46:39.230 --> 00:46:42.210
going to feel so good when someone says yes or something like that.
大概是这样的话。

1087
00:46:42.210 --> 00:46:43.230
No, that's what she says.
不，她就是这么说的。

1088
00:46:43.450 --> 00:46:44.330
She lays it on pretty thick.
她表现得相当露骨。

1089
00:46:44.430 --> 00:46:44.670
Yeah.
是啊。

1090
00:46:45.310 --> 00:46:49.670
And Robert has a talking head where he says he doesn't normally allow sexual desire to
罗伯特有一个独白镜头，他说他通常不允许性欲

1091
00:46:49.670 --> 00:46:55.330
influence his business decisions, but he finds it best to temporarily recuse himself until
影响他的商业决策，但他觉得最好暂时回避一下，直到

1092
00:46:55.330 --> 00:46:59.030
he's made love and then he can revisit the situation rationally.
他做完爱，然后再理智地重新审视这种情况。

1093
00:46:59.170 --> 00:47:01.330
He says Buffett operates the same way.
他说巴菲特也是这样运作的。

1094
00:47:01.330 --> 00:47:01.950
Okay.
好吧。

1095
00:47:02.490 --> 00:47:06.970
I have found the character of Robert California just gets increasingly weirder and weirder.
我发现罗伯特·加利福尼亚这个角色变得越来越古怪了。

1096
00:47:07.130 --> 00:47:11.030
And I got a little curious about it.
我对此感到有点好奇。

1097
00:47:11.310 --> 00:47:13.930
Like, what exactly is going on?
比如，到底发生了什么？

1098
00:47:14.150 --> 00:47:14.570
Why?
为什么？

1099
00:47:14.950 --> 00:47:19.950
And I actually found a quote from James Spader in Andy Green's book.
我实际上在安迪·格林的书中找到了詹姆斯·斯派德的一段引语。

1100
00:47:20.110 --> 00:47:25.190
And I want to read you his take on Robert California getting weirder and weirder.
我想读读他对罗伯特·加利福尼亚变得越来越古怪的看法。

1101
00:47:25.750 --> 00:47:31.130
He said, quote, the characters on the show were constantly treating my character like
他说，引用一下，剧中的角色总是把我的角色当作

1102
00:47:31.130 --> 00:47:34.190
this sort of enigmatic guy who they couldn't quite figure out.
那种他们完全琢磨不透的神秘人物。

1103
00:47:34.190 --> 00:47:38.630
And I realized partway in that the writers couldn't quite figure him out either.
演到一半我意识到，编剧们其实也完全没琢磨透他。

1104
00:47:38.850 --> 00:47:43.230
I mean, the same relationship that the other characters had with Robert, the writers had
我的意思是，其他角色与罗伯特的关系，编剧们

1105
00:47:43.230 --> 00:47:44.030
with him as well.
与他也是一样的。

1106
00:47:44.170 --> 00:47:46.570
But I feel that worked to my advantage.
但我感觉这反而成了我的优势。

1107
00:47:46.930 --> 00:47:51.510
They wrote some really strange, eccentric stuff that I loved goofing around with.
他们写了一些非常奇怪、古怪的东西，我特别喜欢拿来胡闹。

1108
00:47:51.510 --> 00:47:56.050
Now, whether it was successful in terms of the greater context of the whole show, I don't
至于这在整部剧的大背景下是否成功，我

1109
00:47:56.050 --> 00:47:56.310
know.
不知道。

1110
00:47:56.550 --> 00:47:57.830
That wasn't my concern.
那不是我关心的。

1111
00:47:58.150 --> 00:48:01.790
My concern was to try and play this guy and commit to him.
我关心的是努力去扮演这个角色，并全身心投入。

1112
00:48:01.910 --> 00:48:06.610
And to me, he was just this very strange, totally eccentric, enigmatic guy.
对我来说，他就是一个非常奇怪、极其古怪、神秘莫测的人。

1113
00:48:06.790 --> 00:48:09.170
And I think that really comes out in his performance.
我觉得这在他的表演中确实体现出来了。

1114
00:48:09.670 --> 00:48:11.630
And it's what I remember of him.
这也是我对他最深刻的记忆。

1115
00:48:11.830 --> 00:48:14.510
He's one of those actors, and you find them a lot in the theater.
他是那种演员，你在剧院里经常能见到这类人。

1116
00:48:14.750 --> 00:48:18.390
The words that the playwright has written are the law.
剧作家写的台词就是金科玉律。

1117
00:48:19.150 --> 00:48:23.030
And it's your job as the actor to figure out how to make it work.
而作为演员，你的工作就是想办法让它行得通。

1118
00:48:23.270 --> 00:48:24.550
And you make it work.
而且你确实做到了。

1119
00:48:24.830 --> 00:48:30.070
And I just, I really liked that perspective on the character and what he had to say about
我只是，我真的很喜欢他对角色的这种看法，以及他对于

1120
00:48:30.070 --> 00:48:32.130
what he was given to play with.
自己所获角色的评价。

1121
00:48:32.450 --> 00:48:33.530
Yeah, I like that too.
是啊，我也喜欢这一点。

1122
00:48:34.190 --> 00:48:40.150
Well, since Robert has left, now the Nellie-Andy showdown is really going to happen.
好吧，既然罗伯特走了，现在奈莉和安迪的对决真的要上演了。

1123
00:48:40.410 --> 00:48:40.690
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1124
00:48:40.870 --> 00:48:42.410
And we talked about this with Claire.
我们和克莱尔讨论过这个。

1125
00:48:42.630 --> 00:48:46.790
They start going back and forth where she calls on Angela to dock his pay.
他们开始来回交锋，奈莉要求安吉拉扣安迪的工资。

1126
00:48:46.790 --> 00:48:48.050
And Angela's like, on it.
安吉拉说，没问题。

1127
00:48:48.210 --> 00:48:51.370
And then Andy wants Angela to dock Nellie's pay.
然后安迪想让安吉拉扣奈莉的工资。

1128
00:48:51.550 --> 00:48:52.430
She doesn't respond.
她毫无反应。

1129
00:48:52.890 --> 00:48:52.940
Crickets.
鸦雀无声。

1130
00:48:54.430 --> 00:48:58.530
And then ultimately, Nellie's going to threaten to dock Andy's pay $10,000.
最后，奈莉威胁要扣安迪一万美元的工资。

1131
00:48:59.230 --> 00:49:00.490
She starts counting.
她开始倒数。

1132
00:49:00.990 --> 00:49:02.550
Andy leaves hurriedly.
安迪匆忙离开。

1133
00:49:03.230 --> 00:49:03.430
Yeah.
是啊。

1134
00:49:03.730 --> 00:49:04.010
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1135
00:49:04.210 --> 00:49:05.670
He makes up an excuse.
他编了个借口。

1136
00:49:05.670 --> 00:49:07.550
It's in the shooting draft that he has to pee.
剧本初稿里写的是他要去尿尿。

1137
00:49:07.750 --> 00:49:08.190
Oh.
哦。

1138
00:49:08.330 --> 00:49:09.490
He ducks out of the room.
他溜出了房间。

1139
00:49:09.630 --> 00:49:10.050
I see.
我明白了。

1140
00:49:16.790 --> 00:49:18.430
But the ground outside is wet.
但外面的地面是湿的。

1141
00:49:18.870 --> 00:49:21.570
And they had sprinkled raindrops on the car.
他们在车上洒了雨滴。

1142
00:49:22.170 --> 00:49:23.850
Because, you know, the cold open.
因为，你知道，这是开场戏。

1143
00:49:24.150 --> 00:49:24.390
Yeah.
是啊。

1144
00:49:24.710 --> 00:49:25.790
It had stopped raining.
雨已经停了。

1145
00:49:25.970 --> 00:49:27.150
But it was raining earlier.
但之前下过雨。

1146
00:49:27.350 --> 00:49:28.050
Cats and dogs.
倾盆大雨。

1147
00:49:28.450 --> 00:49:31.930
I kind of feel like Erin should have read the room here.
我觉得艾琳当时应该看下气氛的。

1148
00:49:32.070 --> 00:49:34.470
Which, look, I know Erin doesn't read the room well.
当然，我知道艾琳不太会看气氛。

1149
00:49:34.590 --> 00:49:34.890
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1150
00:49:34.990 --> 00:49:38.190
But I think she should have been like, you know, forget about tonight's hot date.
但我觉得她当时应该说，你知道，忘了今晚的约会吧。

1151
00:49:38.770 --> 00:49:39.050
Right.
对。

1152
00:49:39.230 --> 00:49:41.010
You know, a lot happened today.
你知道，今天发生了很多事。

1153
00:49:41.010 --> 00:49:42.930
I can see you're preoccupied.
我看得出你心事重重。

1154
00:49:43.130 --> 00:49:43.490
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1155
00:49:43.490 --> 00:49:44.310
Let's just hang out.
我们就在这儿待着吧。

1156
00:49:44.610 --> 00:49:45.790
Let's just watch a movie.
我们看部电影吧。

1157
00:49:46.310 --> 00:49:46.590
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1158
00:49:47.310 --> 00:49:52.490
But I feel like isn't that kind of maybe what a woman wants at the end of a hard day?
但我觉得，这难道不是女人在辛苦一天后想要的吗？

1159
00:49:52.810 --> 00:49:57.050
Is for her partner to recognize, like, I know what you would love.
就是希望伴侣能懂，比如，我知道你想要什么。

1160
00:49:57.050 --> 00:50:04.570
Is a good snuggle on the couch and a let's binge a show and share a tub of ice cream sort of thing.
就是那种在沙发上依偎在一起，刷刷剧，再分吃一桶冰淇淋的感觉。

1161
00:50:04.710 --> 00:50:09.970
But maybe at the end of a hard day for a man, I know, I'm throwing out stereotypes right now.
但也许男人辛苦一天后，我知道，我现在是在说刻板印象。

1162
00:50:09.970 --> 00:50:12.610
But maybe the man wants the hot date.
但也许男人想要的是一场火热的约会。

1163
00:50:12.850 --> 00:50:13.770
You know what I mean?
你明白我的意思吗？

1164
00:50:13.870 --> 00:50:17.170
How do men who've had a hard day like to finish their day?
辛苦了一天的男人喜欢怎么结束他们的一天呢？

1165
00:50:17.210 --> 00:50:20.410
I'm sure they'll write us and let us know.
我相信他们会写信告诉我们的。

1166
00:50:21.310 --> 00:50:21.750
Okay.
好吧。

1167
00:50:23.310 --> 00:50:27.470
So in the episode that aired, the next scene is the start of a new day.
在播出的那一集中，下一个场景是新的一天的开始。

1168
00:50:27.610 --> 00:50:27.850
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1169
00:50:27.950 --> 00:50:28.170
Right?
对吧？

1170
00:50:28.410 --> 00:50:28.530
Yeah.
是啊。

1171
00:50:28.630 --> 00:50:30.350
It's Erin approaching Andy in the break room.
是艾琳在休息室走近安迪。

1172
00:50:30.550 --> 00:50:33.570
Well, in the producer's cut, there was a scene before it.
嗯，在制片人剪辑版里，在那之前还有一个场景。

1173
00:50:33.770 --> 00:50:34.130
Oh.
哦。

1174
00:50:34.430 --> 00:50:35.610
And I want to share it.
我想分享一下。

1175
00:50:36.470 --> 00:50:41.450
Andy is sort of tucked around the corner of the warehouse, kind of hiding in that alleyway.
安迪躲在仓库的拐角处，藏在那条小巷里。

1176
00:50:41.790 --> 00:50:45.730
And as Dwight, Kevin, and Oscar make their way in for the day, he's like, guys, guys.
当德怀特、凯文和奥斯卡上班走进来时，他喊道：嘿，伙计们，伙计们。

1177
00:50:45.850 --> 00:50:46.790
And he pulls them aside.
他把他们拉到一边。

1178
00:50:47.670 --> 00:50:49.130
And I want you to hear this clip.
我想让你们听听这段录音。

1179
00:50:50.210 --> 00:50:51.310
What are you guys talking about?
你们在聊什么呢？

1180
00:50:51.750 --> 00:50:52.410
Charlie Rose.
查理·罗斯。

1181
00:50:52.810 --> 00:50:53.810
I don't know who that is.
我不知道那是谁。

1182
00:50:53.890 --> 00:50:54.070
Guys.
伙计们。

1183
00:50:54.350 --> 00:50:54.490
He has.
他有。

1184
00:50:54.710 --> 00:50:55.070
Guys.
伙计们。

1185
00:50:58.920 --> 00:50:59.400
What do you?
你们在干嘛？

1186
00:50:59.540 --> 00:51:00.040
Come on.
拜托。

1187
00:51:03.540 --> 00:51:04.380
Where are we going?
我们要去哪儿？

1188
00:51:05.940 --> 00:51:06.300
Okay.
好吧。

1189
00:51:06.880 --> 00:51:07.940
Do you guys want...
你们想不想……

1190
00:51:07.940 --> 00:51:09.500
Andy, you should not stand there.
安迪，你不该站在那儿。

1191
00:51:09.700 --> 00:51:12.220
The warehouse guys pee there all the time.
仓库的人经常在那儿撒尿。

1192
00:51:13.800 --> 00:51:14.140
Ew.
呃。

1193
00:51:16.580 --> 00:51:16.840
Okay.
好吧。

1194
00:51:17.320 --> 00:51:19.280
Do you guys want to be part of something huge?
你们想参与一件大事吗？

1195
00:51:19.560 --> 00:51:21.440
I'm already a member of the largest club there is.
我已经是一个最大俱乐部的成员了。

1196
00:51:21.640 --> 00:51:22.780
Non-church-going Christians.
不去教堂的基督徒。

1197
00:51:25.200 --> 00:51:32.020
You remember in the movie Rudy, when a player comes into the coach's office and he throws his jersey down and he's like,
你记得电影《追梦赤子心》里，当一名球员走进教练办公室，把球衣往地上一摔，说：

1198
00:51:32.160 --> 00:51:33.440
I'm not playing without Rudy.
没有鲁迪我就不打球了。

1199
00:51:33.700 --> 00:51:36.120
And the coach is like, one guy, no big deal.
教练说：一个人而已，没什么大不了的。

1200
00:51:36.120 --> 00:51:40.920
But then every player comes in, one by one, and they all throw their jerseys down for Rudy.
但后来每个球员都一个接一个地走进来，为了鲁迪把球衣都摔在了地上。

1201
00:51:41.180 --> 00:51:41.880
You remember that?
你还记得那个吗？

1202
00:51:42.240 --> 00:51:43.820
Yeah, I remember that.
记得，我记得那个。

1203
00:51:44.540 --> 00:51:53.720
So, how amazing would it be if you guys all did that for me with your own brand new Dunder Mifflin jerseys?
那么，如果你们大家都能穿着全新的邓德·米夫林球衣为我做那件事，该有多棒啊？

1204
00:51:54.220 --> 00:51:55.040
Hey, guys.
嘿，伙计们。

1205
00:51:57.500 --> 00:52:00.660
And then Nate comes in and starts to pee by the wall.
然后内特走进来，开始在墙边撒尿。

1206
00:52:01.540 --> 00:52:05.880
What's so amazing about that is they made Dunder Mifflin jerseys?
那件事最神奇的地方在于，他们真的做了邓德·米夫林的球衣？

1207
00:52:06.040 --> 00:52:06.360
Yes.
是的。

1208
00:52:06.360 --> 00:52:07.160
For the scene?
是为了那个场景吗？

1209
00:52:07.400 --> 00:52:08.620
A whole box of them.
整整一箱呢。

1210
00:52:08.780 --> 00:52:09.560
He holds them up.
他把它们举了起来。

1211
00:52:09.700 --> 00:52:14.120
They're like legit, nice, real, like football jerseys.
它们看起来很正规、很漂亮、很真实，就像橄榄球球衣一样。

1212
00:52:14.300 --> 00:52:15.160
They're navy.
是深蓝色的。

1213
00:52:15.380 --> 00:52:17.080
And in white, they say Dunder Mifflin.
上面用白色印着“邓德·米夫林”。

1214
00:52:17.160 --> 00:52:18.280
I wish I had one.
我真希望我能有一件。

1215
00:52:18.440 --> 00:52:18.680
Yeah.
是啊。

1216
00:52:18.900 --> 00:52:19.760
They're so cute.
它们太可爱了。

1217
00:52:19.940 --> 00:52:24.880
And, lady, I just thought, you know, we had these jerseys made and the storyline got completely cut.
而且，女士，我当时就在想，你知道，我们做了这些球衣，但剧情却被完全删掉了。

1218
00:52:25.220 --> 00:52:27.200
But you can see them throughout the episode.
但你可以在整集里看到它们。

1219
00:52:27.200 --> 00:52:28.160
